      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a lot of nuance. I guess I'm just trying to understand the biological side of it though. When we're talking about \"documenting disparities,\" some of the older studies I've seen actually suggest there are physiological differences in how some populations process opioids or react to inflammatory responses. From a strictly biological or evolutionary standpoint, is there any truth to the idea that different racial groups have inherent anesthetic or pain-response differences, or is it 100% just the social/psychological stuff?",
